Two bags of holding are *not* good. One is better. If you're carrying
more than one, you *will*, eventually, make the mistake of putting one
inside the other, no matter how often you don't make that mistake.

If you have a bag of holding with things you don't really need, you
shouldn't carry all that surplus weight at all. Be more selective in
what you're carrying.

You may also choose to use an (oilskin) sack to put your really
essential items in: should it get cursed, you won't lose anything, and
the things inside will never get cursed anyway.

And lastly, don't use bags of holding as stashes: use a chest for this
purpose. Chests may contain every item, while you may blow up your stash
with a mere wand of cancellation. Just put these extra bags of holding
in your stash-chest.

> Now the problem is the weight of all the food I have to carry around
> to feed my spellcasting habit.  If I could wish for a few hundred
> lumps of bee jelly I might do it :)

My spellcasters (not just wizards) can usually get by easily on corpses,
and carry only *one* food item for emergencies (next to two lizard
corpses and a sprig of wolfsbane for *other* emergencies).

